omponents/button-18","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button","content":"Use the `CloseButton` preset to dismiss an overlay (such as a `Modal`). It defaults to `slot=\"close\"`, so it picks up the overlay's close behavior with no wiring, and always renders an `x` icon with `aria-label=\"Close\"`. For a labelled dismiss action (e.g. \"Cancel\"), use a raw `<Button slot=\"close\">Cancel</Button>`."},"119":{"id":"/docs/components/button-19","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button","content":"Inside a field `Group`, `slot=\"control\"` and `slot=\"trigger\"` pick up the matching look, size, and\ndisabled state from context. See TextField for control affixes, and Select or DatePicker for trigger faces."},"120":{"id":"/docs/components/button-20","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#default","content":"The default/tertiary button is the base for all other buttons in the system. It provides no significant visual treatment other than to provide indication for the user to take a common action."},"121":{"id":"/docs/components/button-21","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#primary","content":"The primary button should be used to indicate the most important action for the user to take in their current experience."},"122":{"id":"/docs/components/button-22","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#secondary","content":"The secondary button indicates an action of secondary importance."},"123":{"id":"/docs/components/button-23","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#tertiary","content":"The tertiary button is the default, low-emphasis style used for common, non-critical actions."},"124":{"id":"/docs/components/button-24","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"te