ay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `Calendar` yourself to replace the whole overlay"],[1549,"**Trigger and options**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders the selected value and a chevron from the field. `SelectOptions` is the list in the popover the Select opens: it takes `ListBox` props (including `items` with a render function for a dynamic collection) plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `ListBox` yourself to replace the whole overlay"],[1109,"**Type to select**: jump to a matching item (string labels are used as `textValue`)"],[959,"**Typed Refs:** Refs are correctly typed based on the `as` value - `useRef<HTMLButtonElement>` works with `as=\"button\"`."],[229,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[779,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[1023,"**Use `Grid` when**: You need explicit two-dimensional layouts with rows and columns, named grid areas, or responsive auto-fill patterns."],[846,"**Use default mode** for SSR applications or when icons appear infrequently"],[847,"**Use sprite mode** when the same icons appear many times (navigation, lists, tables)"],[857,"**Use sprite mode**: For repeated icons, consider sprite mode which consolidates multiple icons into a single SVG sprite sheet, reducing DOM size and improving performance when the same icon appears multiple times"],[1196,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1553,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1779,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1194,"**Value scale**: `minValue`, `maxValue`, `step`, and `formatOptions` configure the numeric behavior"],[284,"**Verify event targets**: Tooltips use mouse event coordinates and bar group positions"],[221,"**Vertical and horizontal orientations**: Choose the best layout for your data and use case"],[260,"**Vertical charts**: Horizontal scrolling when many data points exceed container width"],[230,"**VisX integration**: Leverages VisX primitives for scales, axes, shapes, and responsive layout"],[833,"**What happens with sprite mode:**"],[1640,"`--color-input-background-default`"],[1637,"`--color-input-background-selected`"],[1646,"`--color-input-text-default`"],[1647,"`--ux-1glcx6s`"],[1635,"`--ux-1m9ys0v`"],[1641,"`--ux-1nu8itt`"],[1644,"`--ux-1sbfig8`"],[1638,"`--ux-sywk25`"],[1650,"`--ux-zvaw3s`"],[154,"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."],[1002,"`<Box blockAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[1004,"`<Box inlineAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[998,"`<Box orientation=\"horizontal\">`"],[1000,"`<Box orientation=\"vertical\">`"],[1005,"`<Flex alignItems=\"center\">`"],[1001,"`<Flex direction=\"column\" >`"],[999,"`<Flex direction=\"row\" >`"],[1003,"`<Flex justifyContent=\"center\">`"],[955,"`2xl` - 2x extra large spacing"],[719,"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."],[1814,"`align` centers the parts as well as the text, so a `Tag` eyebrow stays centered too."],[1397,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[1522,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[580,"`aria-describedby` wires the `helperText` to the progressbar for screen readers"],[473,"`aria-disabled` for disabled checkboxes"],[1398,"`aria-disabled` for disabled options"],[1523,"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"],[475,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1400,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1910,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1524,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[579,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[1298,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[474,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1399,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[577,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[1296,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[1295,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value"],[576,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[1297,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"],[578,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[947,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[153,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[241,"`categoryColors` maps individual category values to palette color indices, overriding\nthe series color for just those bars — so a single series can carry a different color\nper category. All three periods here share the same category-to-color map, so each\nchannel keeps one color across every period; the comparison periods are dropped to\nreduced opacity."],[459,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[529,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[547,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[525,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[540,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1952,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[398,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[1332,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[808,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[811,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[807,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[809,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[810,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[812,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1628,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[606,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[639,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[1242,"`Enter/Space`"],[681,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[902,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[648,"`Escape`"],[1169,"`Escape`"],[1244,"`Escape`"],[1957,"`Escape`"],[718,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[984,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[816,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[1022,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[732,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[890,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[919,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[381,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[953,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[1063,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[952,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[1098,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[151,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[609,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[1164,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[1160,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[1331,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[233,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1697,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1947,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[910,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[893,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[1236,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[896,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[1270,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[1275,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1386,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Radio` takes label text next to the indicator. `orientation` also sets keyboard-navigation direction and ARIA."],[400,"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[401,"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."],[399,"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[1171,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[1246,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[652,"`role=\"dialog\"` with `aria-modal=\"true\"` on the drawer panel (via RAC Modal)"],[815,"`role=\"img\"`: When title prop is provided"],[814,"`role=\"presentation\"`: For decorative icons"],[575,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1294,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1396,"`role=\"radio\"` on each option"],[1521,"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"],[1395,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1520,"`role=\