eople expect."],[389,"`xPaddingOuter` and `yPaddingOuter` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."],[950,"`xs` - Extra small spacing"],[236,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - abbreviated dates on one axis, thousands separators on the other. The functions receive the raw accessor value, so they also cover currency, units, or percentages."],[382,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."],[379,"`xTickMarks` and `yTickMarks` draw the short lines at each tick value, which helps tie a label to its exact position on the axis."],[377,"`xTitle` and `yTitle` label what each axis actually measures, e.g. \"Month\" and \"Temperature (°F)\"."],[387,"`xZero` and `yZero` stretch the domain to include zero. Worth doing when the absolute size of the values matters, not just their movement."],[272,"✅ Custom domains"],[273,"✅ Design system alignment"],[1659,"✅ For binary on/off preferences (e.g. Wi-Fi, notifications, dark mode)"],[1913,"✅ For compact action grouping — related actions in space-constrained layouts (e.g. Undo / Redo, Zoom In / Out / Reset)"],[1912,"✅ For grouped contextual actions — two or more closely related actions that belong together (e.g. Bold / Italic / Underline, Align Left / Center / Right)"],[1914,"✅ For multi-select scenarios — when users need to select multiple options simultaneously"],[478,"✅ For selecting multiple independent options"],[1658,"✅ For settings that take effect immediately, without a form submission"],[480,"✅ For toggling settings or features on/off"],[271,"✅ Interactive tooltips"],[270,"✅ Responsive behavior with sticky axes"],[268,"✅ Single and multi-series support"],[269,"✅ Vertical and horizontal orientations"],[481,"✅ When all available options should be visible"],[1402,"✅ When all options should be visible at once"],[1403,"✅ When the decision is important and deserves space"],[1401,"✅ When there are 2-7 mutually exclusive options"],[479,"✅ When users can select zero, one, or many items"],[1405,"❌ For binary yes/no choices (use Checkbox or Toggle instead)"],[1661,"❌ For choosing one of several mutually exclusive options (use `Radio` or `SegmentedController` instead)"],[1916,"❌ For more than 5 choices — cognitive overload; consider a **Select** instead"],[1404,"❌ For more than 7 options (use Select instead)"],[1919,"❌ For mutually exclusive content views (e.g. Monthly / Yearly) — use **SegmentedController** instead"],[482,"❌ For mutually exclusive options (use Radio instead)"],[1660,"❌ For selections that require a \"Save\" or \"Submit\" action (use `Checkbox` instead)"],[483,"❌ For simple on/off toggles without labels (use Toggle/Switch instead)"],[1915,"❌ For unrelated actions that perform disconnected tasks without shared context"],[1917,"❌ When actions require strong visual distinction (e.g. Save vs. Delete)"],[1918,"❌ When selecting an option leads to a different page or workflow — use navigation instead"],[1406,"❌ When space is limited (use Select dropdown)"],[276,"🚧 Additional customization options (tick formatting, axis configuration)"],[274,"🚧 RTL compatibility (axis rendering and spacing refinement)"],[275,"🚧 Tick mark positioning improvements"],[906,"A `<Button slot=\"trigger\">` gets `aria-expanded` + `aria-controls` wired to the `InlineDrawerPanel` automatically (via RAC Disclosure)."],[653,"A `Heading slot=\"title\"` labels the dialog via `aria-labelledby`; otherwise pass `aria-label`"],[1247,"A `Heading slot=\"title\"` labels the dialog via `aria-labelledby`. Without one, a popover inside\na `PopoverTrigger` falls back to being labelled by its trigger; standing alone with\n`triggerRef` it needs an explicit `aria-label`"],[1102,"A `Menu` is a collection, so it only renders `MenuItem`, `MenuGroup`,\n`MenuSeparator`, and `SubmenuTrigger` children. Rich content inside a `Menu`\nor submenu is not supported. To show a `Calendar`, let the item close the\nmenu from `onAction` and open a separate `Popover` anchored to the trigger\nwith `triggerRef`."],[1114,"A `Menu` is a collection: it only renders `MenuItem`, `MenuGroup`,\n`MenuSeparator`, and `SubmenuTrigger`. For rich content (a `Calendar`, a form),\nclose the menu from `onAction` and open a separate `Popover` anchored with\n`triggerRef` instead of putting it in a submenu."],[1101,"A `MenuGroup` with `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` renders its items as checkboxes.\nDrive the checked items with `selectedKeys` + `onSelectionChange` or\nseed them uncontrolled with `defaultSelectedKeys`. Keys correspond to each\n`MenuItem`'s `id`."],[1103,"A `MenuGroup` with `selectionMode=\"single\"` lets one item be selected at a time.\nDrive it with `selectedKeys` + `onSelectionChange` or seed it uncontrolled with\n`defaultSelectedKeys`. Keys correspond to each `MenuItem`'s `id`."],[384,"A `null` Y value breaks the line instead of drawing through the gap, so missing data reads as missing rather than as a straight interpolation."],[243,"A `renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card, using\n`categoryColors` so each date owns its color. Hovering a bar group shows both years'\nvalues and the percent change; the tooltip swatch is resolved per category from the\nhovered datum, demonstrating category colors inside a custom tooltip."],[1883,"A `ToggleButton` toggles between selected and unselected. Wrap multiple inside a `ToggleButtonGroup` to link them with shared selection and keyboard navigation."],[571,"A basic determinate progress indicator with a label and helper text."],[1588,"A binary toggle control that switches a setting between on and off states, communicated via the WAI-ARIA switch role."],[1733,"A bolder color treatment for when tags need to stand out more - for example, on colored backgrounds."],[156,"A calendar with a pre-selected date."],[396,"A categorical X axis (band scale) with several series a